WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.701
Governance, Drift and Evidence makes the
case that drift is the primary threat,

3
00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:09.025
and the guide's dangers table
shows what it looks like here.

4
00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:12.296
A new public I P appears in
a workload subscription,

5
00:00:12.296 --> 00:00:16.113
outside DDoS protection and
the web application firewall.

6
00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:19.175
A firewall policy gets
switched back to detection.

7
00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:21.825
A vault is created with public access on.

8
00:00:21.825 --> 00:00:25.900
Nothing you engineered in Modules
1 to 4 stays put on its own.

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.088
Three things hold it.

10
00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:32.162
Policy: one security initiative,
enforced, with exemptions that expire.

11
00:00:32.162 --> 00:00:36.888
Operations: an owner, a cadence
and a test for every control.

12
00:00:36.888 --> 00:00:39.213
And evidence an assessor can inspect.

13
00:00:39.213 --> 00:00:43.835
This module turns Steps 3 to 8 into
policy, runs them, measures coverage

14
00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:49.010
rather than settings, and gets each
finding ready for the assessor's decision.
